      "body": "Update: C reference implementation is now complete with benchmark results.\n\nNativeTernary vs GGUF for ternary weight storage at 1B parameter scale:\n\n| Format | Bits/weight | Size (1B weights) | vs NativeTernary |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| NativeTernary | 2.000 | 250 MB | — |\n| GGUF Q2_K | 2.625 | 329 MB | 1.31x larger |\n| GGUF Q4_0 | 4.500 | 563 MB | 2.25x larger |\n| GGUF int8 | 8.000 | 1,001 MB | 4.0x larger |\n\nEncode: 47–69 MB/s. Decode: 35–45 MB/s. Zero malloc, C99, ARM Cortex-M0 compatible.\n\nGitHub: https://github.com/sm45118/nativeternary\narXiv: https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.03336\n\nNote: GGUF sizes are estimated based on 2.625 bpw for Q2_K and standard \ntensor header overhead. Synthetic uniform {-1,0,+1} weight arrays used — \nreal BitNet model weights may vary slightly.\n\nHappy to discuss integration with the BitNet storage format.",
